## Overview

`service-opentelemetry` provides two focused modules:

- `services/opentelemetry/api.ts` configures server-side OTLP/HTTP JSON export and same-origin proxy routes for browser traces, metrics, and logs.
- `services/opentelemetry/browser.ts` configures browser OTLP export and captures global errors and unhandled promise rejections as failed spans.

The browser exporter posts to `/api/otel/v1/traces`, `/api/otel/v1/metrics`, and `/api/otel/v1/logs`. The API proxy forwards those requests to `OTEL_COLLECTOR_PROXY_URL`, avoiding browser CORS and collector exposure.

## Server Setup

Merge the application-owned routes, then inject `HttpApiOtlp.layer`. It provides the server OTLP exporter, browser proxy routes, HTTP server services, and tracer suppression for OTLP ingestion:

```ts
import { Layer } from "effect";

import { HttpApiOtlp } from "@/services/opentelemetry/api";

const appRoutes = Layer.mergeAll(apiLayer, docsLayer, mcpLayer);
const appLayer = appRoutes.pipe(
  Layer.provideMerge(HttpApiOtlp.layer),
);
```

## Browser Setup

Install the configured browser layer globally on the Atom runtime used by the application API client. Runtime-level installation is required so browser-only spans are exported as well as propagated to API requests:

```ts
import { Atom } from "effect/unstable/reactivity";

import { BrowserOtlp } from "@/services/opentelemetry/browser";

const apiRuntime = Atom.context();

if (!import.meta.env.SSR) {
  apiRuntime.addGlobalLayer(
    BrowserOtlp.layer({ serviceName: "my-app-web" }),
  );
}

export class ApiClient extends AtomHttpApi.Service<ApiClient>()("ApiClient", {
  api: Api,
  httpClient: FetchHttpClient.layer,
  baseUrl: import.meta.env.VITE_SITE_URL,
  runtime: apiRuntime,
}) {}
```

`BrowserOtlp.layer` accepts optional `serviceVersion`, resource `attributes`, `baseUrl`, and the remaining `Otlp.layerJson` options. The base URL defaults to `/api/otel` and exporter intervals have browser-friendly defaults.

The layer starts when the API runtime atom is read. To start global exception capture during hydration, read it once in the root component:

```tsx
useAtomValue(ApiClient.runtime);
```

## Server Environment Variables

- `OTEL_COLLECTOR_PROXY_URL` - collector base URL used by the browser telemetry proxy
- `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` - server service name
- `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` - server OTLP collector base URL
- `OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp`
- `OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp`
- `OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp`
- `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` - optional server resource attributes
